  "captionStyleReason": "User feedback 2026-08-22: match the caption style to the topic. The locked word-reveal renders small italic serif, which read as documentary over a warm app-discovery reel. chip-lg is bold white SF Pro on a dark pill \u2014 the treatment the reference reel the user sent uses, and legible on mute at thumbnail size.",
  "script": "Your Mac has a third input device.\n\nNot the keyboard. Not the trackpad. The one that's already in your hand.\n\nThis app turns your iPhone into a custom control panel for your Mac.\n\nTap once to open the apps you use every day.\n\nAdd a shortcut, and a whole workflow becomes one button.\n\nSave the sites you always open, and launch them from the same grid.\n\nScroll back through everything you had open, and jump straight to it.\n\nYou can even control windows with gestures.\n\nIt needs a companion app on your Mac and the same Wi-Fi.\n\nBut once it's set up, your most-used actions live right beside your keyboard.\n\nWant the app? Comment APP and we'll send the exact one in your DM.",
